      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>Man in the Moon</head>
        <p>The Man in the Moon</p>
        <p>came down too soon, But said he had come to crave a boon. "A supply of 'Van Houten's ' I beg, quoth he; "There's nothing so good, when hungry you be. "Cold porridge is not at all to my taste, "But good cocoa builds up without any waste.</p>
        <p>"So here's to 'Van Houten '— I've finished, alack 1</p>
        <p>"But now7—a new man— to the 'Moon I'll go back."</p>
      </div>
