      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0012" n="art0012">
        <head>PADGATE.</head>
        <p>PADGATE.</p>
        <p>WESLEYAN Blau CLASS.—Last Sunday afternoon W. S. Wright of Warrington was the speaker who addressed the members of the class. Mr. Councillor Brough occupying the chair—Mr. Wright took for his subject" The Christian Race "basing his remarks upon the teaching's, writings and life of St. Paul, his descrip- tions and illustrations being vivid and apt. Messrs. Hall, Englrnd, London, Seed, Brongh and others after- wards supplimented the remarks by the speaker the result being that an interesting and profitable afternoon was spent.</p>
