      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <p>mcDouGALL's paterit SELF-RAISING FLOUR BEST psAsT The Examiner, Saturday, March 10, 1906. WO-MAN'S REALM. A</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0016" n="art0016">
        <head>DEES3--7,ISTIION-ITOME.</head>
        <p>DEES3--7,ISTIION-ITOME.</p>
        <p>A DDI'M OF UN/ON. Adeline Duchess ol Decll'ord and filo 'Bishop of London have prornisxl to deliver addressee at a meeting at thn7l House. Westminster, for girls only, on March -12th. The object of the gathering will be to interest young ladies of leisure in London in the work of the Girls' Diocesan Association. This was started five years ago to bind together all the girls of the educated classes who, as members of the • Church of England, are willing to help their poorer ! sisters in whatever way lies within their capa- cities.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>CoNnumATiox RESS.</head>
        <p>A CoNnumATiox RESS.</p>
        <p>Confirmation is an important event that comes to many young girls every spring, and during the weeks of preparation that come before the actual ceremony it.. is not unnatural that the maidens should give a good deal of thcught to the toilet to be worn on this occasion. Two things are neces-aty—that the dress be white, and that all elaborateness be strictly avoided. Our sketch shews a simple little Confirmation giress which could be camed ottt in any pretty</p>
        <p>woollen fabric. ' such es Maine, caihmere, and kindred materials. The skirt is laid in box- pleats, prettily stitched down with rows of French knots, the hem being treated in a similar way. The bodice in every way corresponds with the skirt, and even the sleeves are laid in box- pleats, finishing at the elbow in a cuff and frills of silk, while the same silk is tucked to form the little vest and collar.</p>
        <p>..)::‘;,::.".•,:5,:i , 4!"0:-. C—t11:;:j4j1411 ":;,. -:.,,,:! .Y•• 'IA .\,' - . , s , „ a,...,„ • tA ,"‘,4,,,, ahl. (-, . troir 0•-,;M:rik:4 --- 441 • w.--I'*4 '-'" ( •• • i; , ... \ 't N . . k 21-.• 1 \ ‘N -Ac* \\\\'‘,\--, 4,1,-1.- :vor •1 • • 1,:, ' ‘ ~,,,' t` ,::,-,---%,)---",/,.. •.g :,r- - I ,</p>
