      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-03-10_WidnesExaminer_art0067" n="art0067">
        <head>NOTES AND NOTIONS.</head>
        <p>NOTES AND NOTIONS.</p>
        <p>Nearly all the troubles which vex humanity can be traced to yellow metal, yellow labour, or yellow hair —" The Financial News." * * * We understand that Councillor W. J. Wilson has been offered and has accepted the position of Mayor's Auditor lately relinquished by Alderman James Fairclough. * *</p>
        <p>* - Mr. Arthur Henderson, M.P. for Barnard Castle,and the Labour party Whip, has promised to conduct one of the Wesleyan services in the Grand Theatre,Black- pool, during the coming season. The nation is evidently becoming more sober for last year's drink bill showed a decrease of £4,819,221. As the total expenditure on alcholic beverages was £101,167,941 there is still plenty of room for temper- ance effort ! * * * ;.• It is reported that after a sudden shower the other day a Town Councillor was nearly drowned in One of the Sankey-street puddles. A rescue was only effected with difficulty owing to there being no life-belt nearer than Warrington Bridge. * * * Many happy returns to the Mayor and Mayoress, Alderman and Mrs. William Bolton! It was the 25th anniversary of their wedding on Monday last, and we are sure the townspeople will join with us in wishing them both long life and happiness. * * * While 150 people own half England our destitute population including paupers is equal to the entire population of Australia. These startling facts were emphasised by Bishop Thornton in his sermon to men. at Warrington. No wonder that the country is crying for reform !</p>
        <p>I</p>
        <p>Hospital Sunday will be observed on March ISth. he need for liberal contributions. is particularly</p>
        <p>rgent this year as the extension of the Infirmary which has been rendered imperative by the rapidly- increasing demands on the accommodation will soon have to be undertaken.</p>
        <p>* * * A committee consisting of all the members of the Council is to be appointed to consider and report upon the revision of Standing Orders of the Council. Several alterations have been proposed in the lastyear or two, and it is obvious that emendations are neces- several directions. * * * n-man Pierpoint has retired from the Education ltee, and at the Council meeting on Tuesday rere no less than four candidates for the vacant Councillors Joseph, Clegg, Skellanci, and .1i all being put forward. Councilor Joseph the coveted appointment. ** * „ler why the Nightsoil Department wants Lte paste ?" Yet it is among the stores just .ed for. There is no mention of eau de cologne we have often thought, would be a very useful oa to the equipment of the department. by rhinoceros, nine *s4t'Ones in weight, is being at all the social functions at Nairobi, British rim. At a children's party the other day the pet played till he was tired, drank the milk of .ee - iws,and then went to sleep. He is five months old.</p>
